  "lineage": "Grown out of Harlem and downtown New York drag balls from the late 1980s and codified on record by MikeQ, Vjuan Allure and the Qween Beat and Vogue Knights circles from the mid-2000s, ballroom is 128-135 BPM 4/4 house built on a chopped 'Ha' crash sample from Masters at Work's 'The Ha Dance', clattering triplet snare rolls, whistle and chant vocals, and commentator ad-libs cued to runway categories.",
